      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ we wyllað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.13"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc freoman beo on hundrede ⁊ on teoðunge gebroht, þe lade wyrðe beon wylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.13"/> oððon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.14"/> weres wyrðe, gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.15"/> hine hwa teon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.star"/> wylle, ofer þ<hi rend="italic">æt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.star2"/></hi> he byð XIIwintre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.16"/>; oððon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.14"/> he ne beo syððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.star3"/> æniges freorihtes wyrðe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.17"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>Þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc mon beo on teoðunge. We wyllað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc freoman beo on hundrede ⁊ on teoðunge gebroht, ðe lade wyrðe beon wylle oððe weres wyrðe, gyf hine hwa afylle, ofer twelfwintre; oþþe he ne beo æniges [freo]rihtes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.3"/> wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>And we wyllaþ, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc freoman beo on hundrede<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.3-3"/> ⁊ on teoþunge gebroht, þe lade wyrðe beon wille oððe weres wyrðe, gyf hine hwa fylle ofer twelfwintra; oððe he ne beo æniges freorihtes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Et uolumus, ut omnis homo liber in hundreto et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.3-2"/> in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.4"/> decima positus sit, qui purgatione dignus esse uelit aut wera, si quis eum post XII.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.5-2"/> etatis suę annum affligat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.6-2"/> (accuset); uel non sit aliqua liberorum rectitudine dignus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Constituimus etiam, ut omnis liber homo, qui uoluerit esse dignus purgatione et libertate, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.8-2"/> Angli uocant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.9"/> (dicunt) lade þurþe ⁊ þeres þurþe, sit in hundredo et in plegio; aliter si occisus fuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.10"/>, postquam fuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.11"/> duodennis, non erit ulla<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.12"/> liberalitate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_20.lnote.oe.13-2"/> dignus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Uolumus etiam, ut omnis liber sit in centenario et in decimacione positus (quicunque dignus esse uoluerit purgacione aut redempcione, si quis eum peremerit), supra duodecim annos; aut nulla libertatis rectitudine dignus habeatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="20[a]" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="184" ed="#robertson"/>Þæt ælc mon beo on teoðunge. We wyllað þæt ælc freoman beo on hundrede ⁊ on teoðunge gebroht, ðe lade wyrðe beon wylle oððe weres wyrðe, gyf hine hwa afylle<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_20.robnote.fn.1"/>, ofer<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_20.robnote.fn.2"/> twelfwintre; oþþe he ne beo<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_20.robnote.fn.3"/> æniges freorihtes<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_20.robnote.fn.4"/> wyrðe,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="264" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we wyllað þæt ælc freoman beo on hundrede and on teoðunge gebroht, þe lade wyrðe beon wylle oððon weres wyrðe gyf hine hwa teon wylle, ofer þæt he byð XII wintre; oððon he ne beo syððan æniges freorihtes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>beweisrechtes theilhaftig — bezw. [wenn erschlagen, der Bezahlung durch] Wergeld theilhaftig — sein will, in Hundertschaft und in Zehntschaft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_20.lnote.de.6"/> gebracht werde; sonst sei er (späterhin <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) keines Freienrechtes theilhaftig. <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_20.lnote.de.1"/>(Dass jedermann in Zehntschaft sei. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und wir wünschen, dass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_20.lnote.de.2"/> jeder Freie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_20.lnote.de.3"/> über zwölfjährig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_20.lnote.de.4"/> (nachdem er zw. ist <hi rend="italic">G</hi>), welcher, wenn ihn jemand verklagen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_20.lnote.de.5"/> will (niederstreckt <hi rend="italic">B A</hi>), des Reinigungs-</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(That everyone be in a tithing. B) And we will that every free man over twelve years old (once he is twelve, G) who wishes to be entitled to clear himself [if accused] — or [if slain] to have his wergild paid — if anyone wishes to accuse him (strikes him down, B A), be brought into a hundred and into a tithing; otherwise let him (thereafter, G) not be entitled to any free man's rights.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_20.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="185" ed="#robertson"/>Every man shall be in a tithing. It is our desire that every freeman, over twelve years of age, who desires to have the right of exculpation and of being atoned for by the payment of his wergeld, if he is slain<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_20.robnote.n.2"/>, shall be brought within a hundred and a tithing<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_20.robnote.n.3"/>; otherwise he shall not be entitled to any of the rights of a freeman,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>And it is our will that every free man who wishes to be entitled to right of exculpation and to a wergild if anyone slays him,<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_20.whinote.n.3"/> be brought, if he is over twelve years old, into a hundred or tithing; otherwise he is not to be entitled to any rights of free men.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="265" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we desire that every freeman over the age of twelve who wishes to be entitled to swear an oath of exculpation and to be eligible for wergild compensation if he is slain is to be enrolled in a hundred and in a tithing; otherwise, he will not be entitled to any of the rights of a freeman.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_25">Leis Wl 25</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="179"><ref target="clause:Hn_8-1">Hn 8.1–8.3</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘teon’ (accuse; compare Quadr.) against B's ‘afylle’, A's ‘fylle’ (strike down; compare Inst., Consiliatio); perhaps both stood in the archetype, one added later (Liebermann). G's ‘syððan’ and ‘þæt he byð’ are missing from the others. B's heading is red.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 323, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 264, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “|”); AZ: added from Rabin p. 264, October 2026 (Rabin’s note to the translation)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Þæt ælc man beo on teoðunge</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">And: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">teon: afylle B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">wylle: fylle A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þæt he byð: omitted AB</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">surety: In other words, each free person is to have someone to guarantee that they will fulfill their obligations to the court and the community.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q'. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q'. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ac <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ac Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">peruenerit, super <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">peruenerit, super Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi> freo <hi rend="italic">eingeschoben</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">freo inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">duodecim <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">duodecim T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">af. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> ac. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">af. K; ac. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wil. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wil. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oþþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oþþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Quadr.; dagegen zu</hi> afylle <hi rend="italic">in BLd</hi> (fylle <hi rend="italic">A</hi>) <hi rend="italic">vgl. Inst.; Consil. Vielleicht stand im Archetyp beides, eines nachträglich.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Quadr.; on the other hand, for afylle in BLd (fylle A) cf. Inst.; Consil. Perhaps the archetype had both, one of them added later.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þ. he b. <hi rend="italic">fehlt übr. ausser Inst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þ. he b. lacking in the others except Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ra <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ra Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt übrigen.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in the others.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">neuer Satz A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">new sentence A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> hundrde <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from hundrde A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quam <hi rend="italic">Cb Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quam Cb Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uo. <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> di. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uo. Cb; di. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">erit <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erit Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">erit <hi rend="italic">HLb;</hi> erat <hi rend="italic">Di</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erit HLb; erat Di</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">illa <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">illa Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">libertate <hi rend="italic">Cb Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">libertate Cb Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Inst setzt <hi rend="italic">plegio</hi> richtig synonym mit Zehnerschaft; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3 i. l</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inst correctly uses <hi rend="italic">plegio</hi> as a synonym for tithing; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3 i. l</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Zehnerschaft 10f.; Bürgschaft 5c; derselbe Gedanke steht nochmals aus früherer Quelle im nächsten Satze; <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. Einl. n. 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Zehnerschaft 10f.; Bürgschaft 5c; the same idea appears again, from an earlier source, in the next sentence; <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. Introduction n. 18</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 8, 2, vielleicht durch Leis Wl 20, 3. 25, und Inst durch Wl art 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 8, 2, perhaps by Leis Wl 20, 3. 25, and Inst by Wl art 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht unterschieden von <hi rend="italic">ælc</hi> in 20a. Auch III Eg 6 hat <hi rend="italic">ælc</hi>, wo I Atr 1 <hi rend="italic">freoman</hi> liest</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not distinguished from <hi rend="italic">ælc</hi> in 20a. III Eg 6 too has <hi rend="italic">ælc</hi>, where I Atr 1 reads <hi rend="italic">freoman</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. u</hi>. 21²; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> mündig 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. below</hi> 21²; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> mündig 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_20.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sowohl <hi rend="italic">teon wylle</hi> wie <hi rend="italic">afylle</hi> muss der Gesetzgeber im Sinne gehabt haben, da nur zu jenem <hi rend="italic">lad</hi>, nur zu diesem <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> passt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The legislator must have had both <hi rend="italic">teon wylle</hi> and <hi rend="italic">afylle</hi> in mind, since <hi rend="italic">lad</hi> fits only the former and <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> only the latter</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_20.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">I have accepted Schmid’s punctuation as giving the better sense. For a different reading see Liebermann, <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. p. 322, cap. 20 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_20.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Note the difference in the MS readings. Inst. has <hi rend="italic">si occisus fuerit</hi> which agrees with that in B and A; Q has <hi rend="italic">si quis eum affligat</hi> (<hi rend="italic">accuset</hi>) which agrees with that in G. Liebermann suggests that the original text may have contained both readings, since <hi rend="italic">lade wyrðe</hi> suits that in G and Q, <hi rend="italic">weres wyrðe</hi> that in B, A, Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_20.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">on borh</hi> near the end of the clause. Liebermann regards the terms <hi rend="italic">teoðung</hi> and <hi rend="italic">borg</hi> as practically synonymous in Canute’s usage of them and as representing the system later known as frankpledge. <hi rend="italic">on teoðunge</hi> is translated <hi rend="italic">in plegio</hi> in Inst., cf. <hi rend="italic">in plegio liberali</hi>, Hn. 8, 2; <hi rend="italic">in francplegio</hi>, Leis Wl. 25.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_20.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>afylle</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">teon wylle</hi> G; <hi rend="italic">fylle</hi> A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_20.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>ofer</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">o. þæt he byð</hi> G.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_20.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>beo</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">b. syððan</hi> G.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_20.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>freorihtes</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">freo</hi> added in 16th cent. in B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_20.whinote.n.3" n="3" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">464</biblScope></bibl><label>him</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The Nero MS. and <hi rend="italic">Quadripartitus</hi> have instead: “if anyone accuses him”.</seg></note>
      </div>
